# Author: Renato Quagliani (rquaglia@cern.ch)
# Forced Lambda_b0 -> Lambda0(p+ pi-) pi0(gamma gamma), and charge conjugate.
# HELAMP benchmark: alpha(Lambda_b -> Lambda pi0) = -0.89 from
# Mohanta, Giri, Khanna, Phys. Rev. D 63, 074001 (2001), Table 4,
# https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/0006109 . With H+ then H- and unit norm,
# |H+| = sqrt((1+alpha)/2) and |H-| = sqrt((1-alpha)/2).
# The paper does not fix the relative phase; zero is an explicit scenario
# choice. This is a theory benchmark, not a measured decay amplitude.
# The Lambda0 daughter HELAMP is copied from Lb2LambdaGamma_trpol.dec.
# Unit fractions force this chain; they are not physical branching fractions.

Alias Lambdab0_SIGNAL Lambda_b0
Alias aLambdab0_SIGNAL anti-Lambda_b0
ChargeConj Lambdab0_SIGNAL aLambdab0_SIGNAL

Alias Lambda0_SIGNAL Lambda0
Alias aLambda0_SIGNAL anti-Lambda0
ChargeConj Lambda0_SIGNAL aLambda0_SIGNAL

Alias pi0_SIGNAL pi0
ChargeConj pi0_SIGNAL pi0_SIGNAL

Decay Lambdab0_SIGNAL
  1.0 Lambda0_SIGNAL pi0_SIGNAL HELAMP 0.23452079 0.0 0.97211110 0.0;
Enddecay
CDecay aLambdab0_SIGNAL

Decay Lambda0_SIGNAL
  1.0 p+ pi- HELAMP .906 0. .423 0.;
Enddecay
CDecay aLambda0_SIGNAL

Decay pi0_SIGNAL
  1.0 gamma gamma PHSP;
Enddecay

End
